      "status": "preserved"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "source": "Virtual devices support limited zoom ranges when delivering depth data to any output.",
      "ko": "[`ARWorldMap`](arworldmap.md)은 실행 중인 [`ARSession`](arsession.md)의 상태를 캡슐화합니다.",
      "sourceHash": "2554f68e5c72ed213501c51638261a6b5ba2fe3fcf25f28524223839ea57a506",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0002",
      "source": "If a device format has no [`supportedDepthDataFormats`](avcapturedevice/format/supporteddepthdataformats.md), the value of this property is an empty array.",
      "ko": "이 상태에는 사용자가 기기를 이동하는 물리적 공간에 대한 ARKit의 인식(기기의 위치와 방향을 결정하는 데 사용됨)과 세션에 추가된 모든 [`ARAnchor`](aranchor.md) 객체(탐지된 실제 환경 기능이나 앱이 배치한 가상 콘텐츠를 나타낼 수 있는 객체)가 포함됩니다.",
      "sourceHash": "e1404ff08f4d42fd627144370f97bfd25847df08b50f47c67fcf0435424cfd4c",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0001",
      "source": "The presence of one or more ranges where the minimum and maximum zoom factors aren’t equal means the system supports continuous zoom with depth.",
      "ko": "월드맵을 저장하고 이를 사용해 새 세션을 시작하면 앱에 새로운 AR 기능을 추가할 수 있습니다:",
      "sourceHash": "336fd4d703cae644ff42a7e81340a3aaf46b58961ff37313e32f8c864dabc513",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0002",
      "source": "For example, if the value of this property contains the closed ranges `2...2` and `4...4`, the system only allows you to set zoom factors 2 and 4 when you enable depth data delivery.",
      "ko": "For example, if the value of this property contains the closed ranges `2...2` and `4...4`, the system only allows you to set zoom factors 2 and 4 when you enable depth data delivery.",
      "sourceHash": "5fdf2aab93b107e18c26f0b91a8de6efb5fe7785fadc7cbdb3e3b3e6696545b8",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0003",
      "source": "Setting a zoom factor outside these ranges results in an exception.",
      "ko": "Setting a zoom factor outside these ranges results in an exception.",
      "sourceHash": "25b4646757c893b569378e9745988f66b630b79aa8e397b03a52b4516e666592",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0004",
      "source": "Alternatively, a closed range of `2...5` indicates the system supports depth data delivery with zoom factors from 2 to 5.",
      "ko": "Alternatively, a closed range of `2...5` indicates the system supports depth data delivery with zoom factors from 2 to 5.",
      "sourceHash": "1e6cd82a2cec7c99c0def0f311b0e30c7b65cf40916f63379c203ff6d755160f",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0005",
      "source": "You can set a zoom factor outside this range, but results in a loss of depth data.",
      "ko": "You can set a zoom factor outside this range, but results in a loss of depth data.",
      "sourceHash": "c80a65eb529dbedd9462e2f4f567fa50d4ef5c8741be9967e6ae17254b33516a",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0006",
      "source": "Setting the zoom factor back to the supported range resumes depth data delivery.",
      "ko": "Setting the zoom factor back to the supported range resumes depth data delivery.",
      "sourceHash": "807a39dbb55c1757c28d9af3bb3dc40f672a186a5790e81acacf353a2711208f",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0001",
      "source": "When you enable depth data delivery, the effective [`videoZoomFactorUpscaleThreshold`](avcapturedevice/format/videozoomfactorupscalethreshold.md) is `1.0`, which means that all zoom factors that aren’t native zoom factors (see [`virtualDeviceSwitchOverVideoZoomFactors`](avcapturedevice/virtualdeviceswitchovervideozoomfactors.md) and [`secondaryNativeResolutionZoomFactors`](avcapturedevice/format/secondarynativeresolutionzoomfactors.md)) result in digital upscaling.",
      "ko": "When you enable depth data delivery, the effective [`videoZoomFactorUpscaleThreshold`](avcapturedevice/format/videozoomfactorupscalethreshold.md) is `1.0`, which means that all zoom factors that aren’t native zoom factors (see [`virtualDeviceSwitchOverVideoZoomFactors`](avcapturedevice/virtualdeviceswitchovervideozoomfactors.md) and [`secondaryNativeResolutionZoomFactors`](avcapturedevice/format/secondarynativeresolutionzoomfactors.md)) result in digital upscaling.",
      "sourceHash": "41654f31ba5d9f735a9d12f45b2638d732f26716dc281a378f39fb887572845a",
      "status": "failed"
    },
